      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "Let $V=C[-1,1],$ the vector space of functions that are continuous over $[-1,1].$ Given that the inner product on $V$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{-1}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\nfind the orthogonal projection of $f(t)=12{t}^{2}$ onto the subspace spanned by $g(t)=3t-3.$",
      "worked_solution": "The orthogonal projection of $f(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{g(t)\\}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{g(t)}\\,f(t)=\\frac{⟨f(t),g(t)⟩}{⟨g(t),g(t)⟩}\\,g(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),g(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}12{t}^{2}\\cdot (3t-3)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(36{t}^{3}-36{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[9{t}^{4}-12{t}^{3}]_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(9-12)-(9+12) \\\\  & =-24,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨g(t),g(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(3t-3)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(9{t}^{2}-18t+9)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[3{t}^{3}-9{t}^{2}+9t]_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(3-9+9)-(-3-9-9) \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the projection is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{g(t)}\\,f(t) & =\\frac{⟨f(t),g(t)⟩}{⟨g(t),g(t)⟩}\\,g(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{-24}{24}\\cdot (3t-3) \\\\  & =-3t+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
